WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:01.650
- I'm Dr. Roshini Raj.

00:00:01.650 --> 00:00:04.310
I'm an Internist and
Gastroenterologist and

00:00:04.310 --> 00:00:05.950
an Associate Professor of Medicine.

00:00:05.950 --> 00:00:07.310
- I'm Dr. Gail Saltz.

00:00:07.310 --> 00:00:10.180
I am Clinical Associate
Professor of Psychiatry.

00:00:10.180 --> 00:00:13.110
- I am a Family Medicine
Practitioner, and I'm here today

00:00:13.110 --> 00:00:15.200
to talk to you about why
we should not be putting

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:17.130
laundry detergent pods in your mouth.

00:00:17.130 --> 00:00:18.996
I can't believe I have to say this.

00:00:18.996 --> 00:00:21.579
(upbeat music)

00:00:23.598 --> 00:00:26.250
In 2018 already, there's been 39 cases in

00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:29.500
the last two weeks, which
is enormous in comparison

00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:32.160
to previous years, and it's in response to

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:33.520
a prank or a meme.

00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:36.720
- Teenagers, or even adults
have taken this challenge

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:38.980
where they are swallowing detergent pods.

00:00:38.980 --> 00:00:40.470
This is a horrible idea.

00:00:40.470 --> 00:00:42.920
It can be very damaging,
not only to your mouth,

00:00:42.920 --> 00:00:45.660
but to your esophagus and
your stomach, your lungs

00:00:45.660 --> 00:00:48.310
potentially, and in some
cases, it can even be fatal.

00:00:48.310 --> 00:00:50.900
- Long before this challenge was an issue,

00:00:50.900 --> 00:00:55.010
very young children who
came upon a pod were at risk

00:00:55.010 --> 00:00:58.120
for eating it, or swallowing
it because they mistook it

00:00:58.120 --> 00:00:58.953
for a candy.

00:00:58.953 --> 00:01:01.540
- Pretty small and so
like, bite sized, and so

00:01:01.540 --> 00:01:03.810
I think the idea is like,
well, if it's bite sized

00:01:03.810 --> 00:01:05.840
then it can't be that harmful.

00:01:05.840 --> 00:01:09.040
- It's brightly colored, it's
multicolored, it's squishy,

00:01:09.040 --> 00:01:12.490
it has a smooth coating
that can be manipulated.

00:01:12.490 --> 00:01:15.480
People often wanna hold
it, manipulate it, or

00:01:15.480 --> 00:01:16.890
unfortunately, put it in their mouth.

00:01:16.890 --> 00:01:19.940
- The detergent pods contain,
in many cases, either

00:01:19.940 --> 00:01:23.550
bleach like detergents, or
other, what we call surfactants,

00:01:23.550 --> 00:01:26.070
which are very damaging
chemicals when your body

00:01:26.070 --> 00:01:27.200
is exposed to them.

00:01:27.200 --> 00:01:29.770
We have a very delicate
lining of our esophagus and

00:01:29.770 --> 00:01:32.040
our stomach, and even our
mouth, and this can be

00:01:32.040 --> 00:01:34.770
easily burned by these types of chemicals.

00:01:34.770 --> 00:01:36.930
When you first put one of
these pods in your mouth

00:01:36.930 --> 00:01:39.810
it's very likely to explode
because it's just kind of

00:01:39.810 --> 00:01:41.580
contained in a plastic coating.

00:01:41.580 --> 00:01:43.880
- It can dissolve with a
quick bite, and it also

00:01:43.880 --> 00:01:46.790
can dissolve with just
like, mouth moisture.

00:01:46.790 --> 00:01:49.220
So it doesn't necessarily
have to be your chomping

00:01:49.220 --> 00:01:50.053
down on it.

00:01:50.053 --> 00:01:51.680
- And this explosion
in your mouth can cause

00:01:51.680 --> 00:01:54.010
severe burning of the
membranes that are lining

00:01:54.010 --> 00:01:55.150
your mouth and your throat.

00:01:55.150 --> 00:01:57.970
If you then swallow the
pod, it can go on to cause

00:01:57.970 --> 00:02:00.070
severe burning of your esophagus.

00:02:00.070 --> 00:02:02.120
This kind of damage could
even cause a tear in

00:02:02.120 --> 00:02:04.980
your esophagus, or an
actual hole, and long term

00:02:04.980 --> 00:02:08.020
can lead to narrowing or
stricturing of the esophagus.

00:02:08.020 --> 00:02:10.090
It can really irritate
or burn the lining of

00:02:10.090 --> 00:02:13.180
your stomach, and irritate
your intestines as well.

00:02:13.180 --> 00:02:15.520
- When you're taking a bite
of it, if you actually end up

00:02:15.520 --> 00:02:18.230
inhaling it, then you can get
some of the laundry detergent

00:02:18.230 --> 00:02:20.830
into your lungs and at
that point it can irritate

00:02:20.830 --> 00:02:23.910
sort of the lung lining,
causing you to cough, wheeze,

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:26.230
have shortness of breath,
and in some really serious

00:02:26.230 --> 00:02:28.700
incidences can cause sort
of inflammation of the lungs

00:02:28.700 --> 00:02:31.490
leading to pulmonary edema,
which is water in the lungs,

00:02:31.490 --> 00:02:34.390
and acute respiratory distress
syndrome, where there's

00:02:34.390 --> 00:02:36.990
too much inflammation for
you to be able to breathe.

00:02:36.990 --> 00:02:41.990
- Taking a high risk prank
to the nth degree is not new.

00:02:43.550 --> 00:02:47.280
Young adults are very drawn
to high risk behaviors

00:02:47.280 --> 00:02:48.860
for biological reasons.

00:02:48.860 --> 00:02:51.060
The amygdala sort of says
to the rest of the brain,

00:02:51.060 --> 00:02:53.950
hey that felt good, let's
do it again, which is why

00:02:53.950 --> 00:02:57.820
this age group has a particular
risk for doing things

00:02:57.820 --> 00:03:00.720
that otherwise they
might deem a poor idea.

00:03:00.720 --> 00:03:03.320
- This is such a disturbing
trend on many levels,

00:03:03.320 --> 00:03:05.100
I think, because of social media.

00:03:05.100 --> 00:03:07.630
Teenagers are doing a
lot of things that maybe

00:03:07.630 --> 00:03:09.370
they wouldn't have done
20 years ago, just 'cause

00:03:09.370 --> 00:03:10.970
they don't have an audience for it.

00:03:10.970 --> 00:03:13.540
- So the same dynamic can
be at play, for example,

00:03:13.540 --> 00:03:16.460
with something like the ALS
bucket challenge, where,

00:03:16.460 --> 00:03:18.780
you know, where like wildfire, it took on.

00:03:18.780 --> 00:03:22.160
It's simply the phenomenon
that large groups can see

00:03:22.160 --> 00:03:25.610
an activity and can get
feedback for that activity

00:03:25.610 --> 00:03:28.100
much more quickly because of social media.

00:03:28.100 --> 00:03:30.910
- You absolutely can die from ingesting

00:03:30.910 --> 00:03:32.390
laundry detergent pods.

00:03:32.390 --> 00:03:35.340
For adults, it's not
necessarily gonna be the pods

00:03:35.340 --> 00:03:37.700
themselves that lead to the risk of death.

00:03:37.700 --> 00:03:40.480
Meaning you can get seizures,
you can get pulmonary edema,

00:03:40.480 --> 00:03:43.260
or you can just have a
significant infection that can

00:03:43.260 --> 00:03:44.150
develop as well.

00:03:44.150 --> 00:03:46.220
- If you're worried about
someone you know potentially

00:03:46.220 --> 00:03:48.550
swallowing a pod, certain
symptoms to look out for are:

00:03:48.550 --> 00:03:52.070
abdominal pain, vomiting, nausea, fever.

00:03:52.070 --> 00:03:55.530
- Right away, you wanna drink
a glass of water, you wanna

00:03:55.530 --> 00:03:57.930
drink some milk to dilute the detergent.

00:03:57.930 --> 00:04:00.690
You want to call poison
control right away.

00:04:00.690 --> 00:04:03.720
Make sure to have details:
what was actually ingested,

00:04:03.720 --> 00:04:05.950
the concentration, the ingredients.

00:04:05.950 --> 00:04:08.640
You really don't want to make them vomit.

00:04:08.640 --> 00:04:11.070
That can actually lead to
aspiration of the own vomit,

00:04:11.070 --> 00:04:12.280
or choking on your own vomit.

00:04:12.280 --> 00:04:14.530
But if any of the symptoms
ever get really serious,

00:04:14.530 --> 00:04:18.020
you have to call 911 and get
to the closest emergency room.

00:04:18.020 --> 00:04:19.940
- If you make something taboo, that's

00:04:19.940 --> 00:04:21.400
simply gonna stoke them.

00:04:21.400 --> 00:04:25.540
An adolescent and young adult,
this desire to take risk,

00:04:25.540 --> 00:04:30.470
this desire to be anti
authoritarian may promote the desire

00:04:30.470 --> 00:04:31.460
to do just that.

00:04:31.460 --> 00:04:34.940
When these kinds of trends
come up, watching media,

00:04:34.940 --> 00:04:38.160
you would have the feeling that
everybody's doing something.

00:04:38.160 --> 00:04:40.560
Hey, everybody's doing
it, it must be okay.

00:04:40.560 --> 00:04:44.350
Really look at the numbers,
which do remain very small.

00:04:44.350 --> 00:04:45.470
Therefore keep that in mind.

00:04:45.470 --> 00:04:49.040
- Please do not put laundry
detergent pods in your mouth,

00:04:49.040 --> 00:04:52.010
even if you think it's
funny, if someone dares you,

00:04:52.010 --> 00:04:54.950
whatever it may be, if
it reminds you of candy.

00:04:54.950 --> 00:04:55.881
Just don't do it.

00:04:55.881 --> 00:04:58.464
(upbeat music)

